<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Genoa</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Genoese</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Genoa is a port city in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> and was a powerful maritime republic in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>. Genoese merchants traded with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayyubid-empire">Ayyubid Empire</a>, held major commercial privileges in the late <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a>, and Genoese bankers financed the campaigns of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/genoa.jpg" alt="Genoa" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Julian Lupyan · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Piazza_de_Ferrari,_Genoa.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
